Package: zucrypt
Title: Cryptography Without System Dependencies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("The Mbed TLS Contributors", role = "cph",
           comment = "TF-PSA-Crypto, bundled in src/vendor/tf-psa-crypto"))
Description: Cryptographic functions over raw vectors, including message
    digests of in-memory data, files and connections, keyed-hash message
    authentication codes (HMAC), Advanced Encryption Standard (AES)
    encryption, constant-time comparison and hexadecimal encoding, backed
    by a bundled and pinned copy of the 'Mbed TLS' project's cryptography
    library, 'TF-PSA-Crypto' (<https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/TF-PSA-Crypto>).
    No system cryptographic library, 'Java' or 'Python' is required at
    install or run time. Algorithm names are matched exactly, and failures
    are reported as structured conditions. The same primitives, and secure
    erasure of native buffers, are published to other packages as a static
    archive and as a registered C interface, so that a package can call
    them from C without going through R.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Copyright: See inst/COPYRIGHTS and tools/vendor/manifest.tsv.
URL: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zucrypt,
    https://pedrobtz.github.io/zucrypt/
BugReports: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zucrypt/issues
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports: 
    utils
Suggests: 
    openssl,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: A C99 compiler. No system cryptographic library is
    used, no CMake, Python or Perl is required, and nothing is downloaded or
    generated during installation: the backend is built from vendored
    sources, with an explicit object list in portable make.
Config/Needs/website: 
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/testthat/parallel: true
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
